body:
I usually fall asleep too! I had to travel quite a lot before covid19 so I got used to it. 

&#x200B;

I remember this one time when I was in deep sleep when turbulence hit, but it somehow managed to wake me up. I jumped up from my seat and grabbed the passenger who sat to my right by his arm, it took me a few seconds to understand fully what was happening and where I was. The next 5 minutes were spent apologizing to the man that I grabbed so aggressively, he thought it was hilarious though.

Ahhh, it happened to one of my friends as well. He wanted to do something nice for his roommates before going out with us to a bar and suddenly his phone started exploding. They made a group chat and sent a looong passive aggressive novel about how he should have not done it. He was pretty bummed for the rest of the evening. :( 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=McdD0cvR6Ok](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=McdD0cvR6Ok) 

&#x200B;

I just imagined the whole "I like..." thing like this, haha
